.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBFloatingIndicator\fR: a row of children with a highlight that slides behind the active one, after Mantine's FloatingIndicator (its tabs' "custom variants"). The children are the app's own widgets, usually flat buttons; the widget only places them in a row and draws the highlight, which eases to the active child's place with the theme's \fBselection\fR motion (instant under reduced motion).
.PP
.nf
.RS
FloatingIndicator::new(
    vec![
        flat_button(label("Preview")).on_press(Msg::Tab(0)).into(),
        flat_button(label("Code")).on_press(Msg::Tab(1)).into(),
    ],
    self.tab,                 // controlled: the app owns the active index
)
.RE
.fi
.PP
The highlight is the window foreground at 10% by default; \fBcolor\fR sets another and \fBradius\fR its corners.
